From: System Electronics
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: force stop state while the PHY comes up

The lanes follow whatever the PHY drives while it is powered up and taken
out of reset, so the link can start from an undefined state.

Backport of Tomi Valkeinen's "drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: Fix stop-state at
enable time", adapted to this driver: the force bits are raised before the
DPHY configuration and dropped 100 us after the reset lines are released.

Upstream-Status: Backport

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -861,12 +861,17 @@
 static void cdns_dsi_hs_init(struct cdns_dsi *dsi)
 {
 	struct cdns_dsi_output *output = &dsi->output;
-	u32 status, stale;
+	u32 status, stale, main_en;
 	int i, ret;
 	
 	if (dsi->phy_initialized)
 		return;
 
+	/* Force the stop state on all lanes while the PHY comes up. */
+	main_en = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN);
+	writel(main_en | DATA_FORCE_STOP | CLK_FORCE_STOP,
+	       dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN);
+
 	/*
 	 * Power all internal DPHY blocks down and maintain their reset line
 	 * asserted before changing the DPHY config.
@@ -896,6 +901,11 @@
 	       DPHY_D_RSTB(output->dev->lanes) | DPHY_C_RSTB,
 	       dsi->regs + MCTL_DPHY_CFG0);
 
+	/* Keep the stop state for at least 100 us, then release it. */
+	usleep_range(100, 200);
+	writel(main_en & ~(DATA_FORCE_STOP | CLK_FORCE_STOP),
+	       dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN);
+
 	dsi->phy_initialized = true;
 }
 
